ceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":16659,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"REV","canonicalOSIS":"Rev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Rev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Rev.6.1-8.1","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Rev.6.1-8.1","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Rev.8.1","r":"Rev.8.1","rawR":"Rev.8.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.8.1","value":"Rev.8.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:1"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The opening of ",{"c":["the seventh seal"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," concludes the first act and dramatically initiates ",{"c":["silence"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," which suggests the mystery of God in his dealings with the world (",{"href":"?bref=Rev.10.4","r":"Rev.10.4","rawR":"Rev.10.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.10.4","value":"Rev.10.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.19.11-12","r":"1Kgs.19.11-12","rawR":"1Kgs.19.11-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.19.11-12","value":"1Kgs.19.11-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 19:11-12"},"). Perhaps the mysterious silence here is analogous to God’s rest on the seventh day of creation (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.2.1-3","r":"Gen.2.1-3","rawR":"Gen.2.1-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.2.1-3","value":"Gen.2.1-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gen 2:1-3"},"; see also ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.4.1-11","r":"Heb.4.1-11","rawR":"Heb.4.1-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.4.1-11","value":"Heb.4.1-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 4:1-11"},"). • ",{"c":["half an hour:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," This brief hush precedes the unfolding of the second act of divine judgment when God will answer the prayers of his people."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Rev.8.1","refs":[{"book":"REV","endChapter":8,"endVerse":1,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Rev.8.1","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"REV","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"004deee75432bf491a2d6309e6aea049d41c9383801b6d4f3c2dc2c401ed8bf3","sourceItemName":"Rev.8.1","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":16683,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"REV","canonicalOSIS":"Rev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Rev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Rev.8.1","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Rev.8.1","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Rev.8.2-11.19","r":"Rev.8.2-11.19","rawR":"Rev.8.2-11.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.8.2-11.19","value":"Rev.8.2-11.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:2–11:19"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The second cycle of judgments is structured around ",{"c":["seven trumpets"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},". Like the first cycle (",{"href":"?bref=Rev.6.1-8","r":"Rev.6.1-8","rawR":"Rev.6.1-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.6.1-8","value":"Rev.6.1-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:1–8:1"},"), this one contains an interlude (",{"href":"?bref=Rev.10.1-11.14","r":"Rev.10.1-11.14","rawR":"Rev.10.1-11.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.10.1-11.14","value":"Rev.10.1-11.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:1–11:14"},"; cp. ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.7.1-17","r":"Rev.7.1-17","rawR":"Rev.7.1-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.7.1-17","value":"Rev.7.1-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:1-17"},") and ends with a glimpse of God’s eternal Kingdom (",{"href":"?bref=Rev.11.15-19","r":"Rev.11.15-19","rawR":"Rev.11.15-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.11.15-19","value":"Rev.11.15-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"11:15-19"},"; see ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.7.9-8.1","r":"Rev.7.9-8.1","rawR":"Rev.7.9-8.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.7.9-8.1","value":"Rev.7.9-8.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:9–8:1"},"). • The trumpet judgments are reminiscent of the ten plagues of Egypt (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.7.14-11.10","r":"Exod.7.14-11.10","rawR":"Exod.7.14-11.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.7.14-11.10","value":"Exod.7.14-11.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 7:14–11:10"},") and have the same purpose—to show the powerlessness of earthly gods (or satanic powers) and to demonstrate beyond doubt the power and sovereignty of God."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Rev.8.2-11.19","refs":[{"book":"REV","endChapter":9,"endVerse":21,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":6}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Rev.8.2-11.19","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"REV","sourceChapterCoverage":[8,9],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"9a0241700220c81467f6242cff140418b3701feb2848f6be025cb35e4f96b4d9","sourceItemName":"Rev.8.2-11.19","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":16684,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"REV","canonicalOSIS":"Rev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Rev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Rev.8.6-9.21","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Rev.8.2-11.19","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Rev.8.2-6","r":"Rev.8.2-6","rawR":"Rev.8.2-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.8.2-6","value":"Rev.8.2-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:2-6"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This scene of preparation in heaven introduces the seven trumpets of judgment and continues the theme of God’s receiving and answering prayer (",{"href":"?bref=Rev.5.8","r":"Rev.5.8","rawR":"Rev.5.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.5.8","value":"Rev.5.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.6.9-11","r":"Rev.6.9-11","rawR":"Rev.6.9-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.6.9-11","value":"Rev.6.9-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:9-11"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Rev.8.2-6","refs":[{"book":"REV","endChapter":8,"endVerse":6,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":2}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Rev.8.2-6","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"REV","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"39099513b0289be0904b0274e53c21435c4a626dc33df69d6a2ce9857c7b9d1a","sourceItemName":"Rev.8.2-6","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":16685,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"REV","canonicalOSIS":"Rev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Rev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Rev.8.2-6","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Rev.8.2-6","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Rev.8.2","r":"Rev.8.2","rawR":"Rev.8.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.8.2","value":"Rev.8.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:2"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The dramatic sounding of ",{"c":["trumpets"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," by ",{"c":["angels"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," heralds an approaching end (see ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.27.13","r":"Isa.27.13","rawR":"Isa.27.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.27.13","value":"Isa.27.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isa 27:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Zech.9.14","r":"Zech.9.14","rawR":"Zech.9.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zech.9.14","value":"Zech.9.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zech 9:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.24.31","r":"Matt.24.31","rawR":"Matt.24.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.24.31","value":"Matt.24.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Matt 24:31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.15.52","r":"1Cor.15.52","rawR":"1Cor.15.52","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.15.52","value":"1Cor.15.52"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 15:52"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Thes.4.16","r":"1Thes.4.16","rawR":"1Thes.4.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Thes.4.16","value":"1Thes.4.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Thes 4:16"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Rev.8.2","refs":[{"book":"REV","endChapter":8,"endVerse":2,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":2}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Rev.8.2","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"REV","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"cba4dd9bbdfc8b66d766f3b71996e54548dc3598537cdff89d93bbdc915a99a9","sourceItemName":"Rev.8.2","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":16686,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"REV","canonicalOSIS":"Rev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Rev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Rev.8.2","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Rev.8.2","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Rev.8.3-4","r":"Rev.8.3-4","rawR":"Rev.8.3-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.8.3-4","value":"Rev.8.3-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:3-4"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["The prayers of God’s people"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," ask for God’s ultimate justice and judgment (",{"href":"?bref=Rev.6.10-11","r":"Rev.6.10-11","rawR":"Rev.6.10-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.6.10-11","value":"Rev.6.10-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:10-11"},"; see also ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.5.8","r":"Rev.5.8","rawR":"Rev.5.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.5.8","value":"Rev.5.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.9.5-6","r":"Ezra.9.5-6","rawR":"Ezra.9.5-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.9.5-6","value":"Ezra.9.5-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezra 9:5-6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.141.2","r":"Ps.141.2","rawR":"Ps.141.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.141.2","value":"Ps.141.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 141:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Dan.9.21","r":"Dan.9.21","rawR":"Dan.9.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Dan.9.21","value":"Dan.9.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dan 9:21"},"). The mixture of ",{"c":["incense"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," and ",{"c":["prayers"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," that reaches God’s presence shows that God hears their prayers (see ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.6.9-11","r":"Rev.6.9-11","rawR":"Rev.6.9-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.6.9-11","value":"Rev.6.9-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rev 6:9-11"},") and is prepared to act."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Rev.8.3-4","refs":[{"book":"REV","endChapter":8,"endVerse":4,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":3}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Rev.8.3-4","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"REV","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"5e51247bcea9b34fd235476c189d7fb71a80d3236a589430ef6b8d351454ad0a","sourceItemName":"Rev.8.3-4","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":16687,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"REV","canonicalOSIS":"Rev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Rev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Rev.8.3-4","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Rev.8.3-4","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Rev.8.5","r":"Rev.8.5","rawR":"Rev.8.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.8.5","value":"Rev.8.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:5"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The action of ",{"c":["the angel,"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," as he throws ",{"c":["fire"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," ",{"c":[". . ."],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"},{"c":[" down upon the earth,"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," signals the dramatic beginning of God’s judgment (see ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.19.24","r":"Gen.19.24","rawR":"Gen.19.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.19.24","value":"Gen.19.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gen 19:24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.9.23","r":"Exod.9.23","rawR":"Exod.9.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.9.23","value":"Exod.9.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 9:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.10.2","r":"Lev.10.2","rawR":"Lev.10.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.10.2","value":"Lev.10.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lev 10:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.9.3","r":"Deut.9.3","rawR":"Deut.9.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.9.3","value":"Deut.9.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Deut 9:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.1.10","r":"2Kgs.1.10","rawR":"2Kgs.1.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.1.10","value":"2Kgs.1.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 1:10"},"). • ",{"c":["thunder . . . lightning . . . earthquake:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," These earthly portents remind us of God’s power, presence, and judgment (also ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.11.19","r":"Rev.11.19","rawR":"Rev.11.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.11.19","value":"Rev.11.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rev 11:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.16.18","r":"Rev.16.18","rawR":"Rev.16.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.16.18","value":"Rev.16.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"16:18"},"; see ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.19.18-19","r":"Exod.19.18-19","rawR":"Exod.19.18-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.19.18-19","value":"Exod.19.18-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 19:18-19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.19.11-12","r":"1Kgs.19.11-12","rawR":"1Kgs.19.11-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.19.11-12","value":"1Kgs.19.11-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 19:11-12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.29.6","r":"Isa.29.6","rawR":"Isa.29.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.29.6","value":"Isa.29.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isa 29:6"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Rev.8.5","refs":[{"book":"REV","endChapter":8,"endVerse":5,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":5}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Rev.8.5","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"REV","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"efa28582847f9b30f3d5bdad5e5c7ad0a93e07d85fc6af2c76a25a73a5967705","sourceItemName":"Rev.8.5","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":16688,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"REV","canonicalOSIS":"Rev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Rev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Rev.8.5","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Rev.8.5","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Rev.8.7-12","r":"Rev.8.7-12","rawR":"Rev.8.7-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.8.7-12","value":"Rev.8.7-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:7-12"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," Each of the first four trumpets affects ",{"c":["one-third"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," of its target (see ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.5.1-4","r":"Ezek.5.1-4","rawR":"Ezek.5.1-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.5.1-4","value":"Ezek.5.1-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezek 5:1-4"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.5.12","r":"Ezek.5.12","rawR":"Ezek.5.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.5.12","value":"Ezek.5.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Zech.13.8","r":"Zech.13.8","rawR":"Zech.13.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zech.13.8","value":"Zech.13.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zech 13:8"},"). The point is not to convey an exact measurement; instead, it indicates that God’s judgment on the earth is beginning but has not reached its zenith. Together, the first four trumpets form a unified message of judgment on the whole physical world (as with ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.6.1-8","r":"Rev.6.1-8","rawR":"Rev.6.1-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.6.1-8","value":"Rev.6.1-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rev 6:1-8"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Rev.8.7-12","refs":[{"book":"REV","endChapter":8,"endVerse":12,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":7}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Rev.8.7-12","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"REV","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"970c44465f5d29c4d6620ba4650dc9a1f2cc00ca767efa02ac4831cfa1210c8c","sourceItemName":"Rev.8.7-12","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":16689,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"REV","canonicalOSIS":"Rev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Rev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Rev.8.7-12","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Rev.8.7-12","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Rev.8.7","r":"Rev.8.7","rawR":"Rev.8.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.8.7","value":"Rev.8.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:7"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["Hail and fire mixed with blood"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," signal the destruction of plant life, as did the seventh plague on Egypt (see ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.9.13-35","r":"Exod.9.13-35","rawR":"Exod.9.13-35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.9.13-35","value":"Exod.9.13-35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 9:13-35"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Joel.2.31","r":"Joel.2.31","rawR":"Joel.2.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Joel.2.31","value":"Joel.2.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Joel 2:31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.2.19","r":"Acts.2.19","rawR":"Acts.2.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.2.19","value":"Acts.2.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 2:19"},"). • ",{"c":["all the green grass was burned:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," Nothing escapes God’s judgment. • This vision need not be harmonized with ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.9.4","r":"Rev.9.4","rawR":"Rev.9.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.9.4","value":"Rev.9.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rev 9:4"}," because each scene is self-contained and communicates its own message."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Rev.8.7","refs":[{"book":"REV","endChapter":8,"endVerse":7,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":7}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Rev.8.7","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"REV","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"96772789c173e73201e87d523412b2556086b830c97a1a00f66c4cfbb4fe4856","sourceItemName":"Rev.8.7","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":16690,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"REV","canonicalOSIS":"Rev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Rev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Rev.8.7","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Rev.8.7","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Rev.8.8-9","r":"Rev.8.8-9","rawR":"Rev.8.8-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.8.8-9","value":"Rev.8.8-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:8-9"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["water . . . became blood:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," This judgment is similar to the first plague on Egypt (see ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.7.14-25","r":"Exod.7.14-25","rawR":"Exod.7.14-25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.7.14-25","value":"Exod.7.14-25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 7:14-25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.78.44","r":"Ps.78.44","rawR":"Ps.78.44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.78.44","value":"Ps.78.44"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 78:44"},"). • The ",{"c":["mountain of fire"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," suggests something similar to the eruption of Mount Vesuvius in ",{"c":["AD"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," 79 that brought bloody destruction to ships and sea life (see Pliny the Younger, ",{"c":["Letters"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," 6.16.1-22)."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Rev.8.8-9","refs":[{"book":"REV","endChapter":8,"endVerse":9,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":8}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Rev.8.8-9","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"REV","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b79ea7c914d5390ad2066dfb71f14e5aac94189d8a4bbff16f87db31746f62cd","sourceItemName":"Rev.8.8-9","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":16691,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"REV","canonicalOSIS":"Rev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Rev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Rev.8.8-9","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Rev.8.8-9","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Rev.8.10-11","r":"Rev.8.10-11","rawR":"Rev.8.10-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.8.10-11","value":"Rev.8.10-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:10-11"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The ",{"c":["star"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," named ",{"c":["Bitterness"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (literally ",{"c":["wormwood,"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," a shrubby plant yielding a bitter extract) is symbolic rather than physical. Bitter water is connected with judgment from early in Israel’s national experience (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.15.22-26","r":"Exod.15.22-26","rawR":"Exod.15.22-26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.15.22-26","value":"Exod.15.22-26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 15:22-26"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.5.18","r":"Num.5.18","rawR":"Num.5.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.5.18","value":"Num.5.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Num 5:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.9.13-16","r":"Jer.9.13-16","rawR":"Jer.9.13-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.9.13-16","value":"Jer.9.13-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 9:13-16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.23.15","r":"Jer.23.15","rawR":"Jer.23.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.23.15","value":"Jer.23.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"23:15"},"). The message is that wide-scale judgment has begun."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Rev.8.10-11","refs":[{"book":"REV","endChapter":8,"endVerse":11,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":10}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Rev.8.10-11","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"REV","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"8ab1dd2b080859462ad70b4fa2af39e1f969de3a2b4935bc4043e1c07e47e3e0","sourceItemName":"Rev.8.10-11","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":16692,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"REV","canonicalOSIS":"Rev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Rev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Rev.8.10-11","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Rev.8.10-11","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Rev.8.12","r":"Rev.8.12","rawR":"Rev.8.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.8.12","value":"Rev.8.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:12"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["the fourth angel:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," On the fourth day of creation, God made ",{"c":["the sun"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," ",{"c":[". . ."],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"},{"c":[" the moon, and"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," ",{"c":[". . ."],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"},{"c":[" the stars"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.1.14-19","r":"Gen.1.14-19","rawR":"Gen.1.14-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.1.14-19","value":"Gen.1.14-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gen 1:14-19"},"). • ",{"c":["the day was dark:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," This judgment replicates the ninth plague in Egypt (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.10.21-23","r":"Exod.10.21-23","rawR":"Exod.10.21-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.10.21-23","value":"Exod.10.21-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 10:21-23"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Rev.8.12","refs":[{"book":"REV","endChapter":8,"endVerse":12,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":12}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Rev.8.12","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"REV","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"dc0a6cd046f74476c7a844a702551e1039e9ddbfaea0038f370890cabb5a6895","sourceItemName":"Rev.8.12","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":16693,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"REV","canonicalOSIS":"Rev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Rev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Rev.8.12","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Rev.8.12","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Rev.8.13","r":"Rev.8.13","rawR":"Rev.8.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.8.13","value":"Rev.8.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:13"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The ancients regarded the ",{"c":["eagle"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," as a symbolic messenger of God (see ",{"c":["4 Ezra"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," 11:7-8; ",{"c":["2 Baruch"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," 77:19-26). • ",{"c":["Terror, terror, terror:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," A threefold announcement would be recognized as a message from God (see ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.10.16","r":"Acts.10.16","rawR":"Acts.10.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.10.16","value":"Acts.10.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 10:16"},"). • The ",{"c":["terror"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (Greek ",{"c":["ouai"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"},") that sounded like an eagle’s screech was directed against humans of ",{"c":["this world"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," who were not among God’s faithful people (",{"href":"?bref=Rev.6.10","r":"Rev.6.10","rawR":"Rev.6.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.6.10","value":"Rev.6.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rev 6:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.9.4","r":"Rev.9.4","rawR":"Rev.9.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.9.4","value":"Rev.9.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:4"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.9.20","r":"Rev.9.20","rawR":"Rev.9.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.9.20","value":"Rev.9.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"20"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Rev.8.13","refs":[{"book":"REV","endChapter":8,"endVerse":13,"startChapter":8,"startVerse":13}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Rev.8.13","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"REV","sourceChapterCoverage":[8],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"32b15b8a6d7418223bff11f43ccec20c4cff5abf8b4df20be6e490ab5c9c1fab","sourceItemName":"Rev.8.13","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":16694,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"REV","canonicalOSIS":"Rev","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Rev"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Rev.8.13","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Rev.8.13","type":"StudyNote"}],"version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}